WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.146
In 2000, Taiwan held another presidential election.

00:00:04.146 --> 00:00:07.710
This election was fiercely contested.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.082
Campaign rallies filled the streets, one after another.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:14.681
Three main candidates competed for voters' support.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:17.838
The televised debate drew many viewers.

00:00:17.838 --> 00:00:21.393
Supporters waved flags and cheered for their candidates.

00:00:21.393 --> 00:00:24.558
On voting day, people braved the rain to vote.

00:00:24.558 --> 00:00:28.547
Everyone hoped their vote would make a difference.

00:00:28.547 --> 00:00:32.084
The count was very close, and everyone held their breath.

00:00:32.084 --> 00:00:34.932
In the end, Chen Shui-bian won the election.

00:00:34.932 --> 00:00:39.281
When the result was announced, some cheered and some were disappointed.

00:00:39.281 --> 00:00:42.428
The ruling party peacefully handed over power.

00:00:42.428 --> 00:00:45.339
It was Taiwan's first transfer of presidential power between parties.

00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:49.076
At the ceremony, the new president waved to the people.

00:00:49.076 --> 00:00:53.115
The peaceful transfer of power became a key sign of democracy.

00:00:53.115 --> 00:00:56.289
Taiwan's democracy had taken another step forward.
